    "updated_at": "2017-07-06T04:36:06Z",
    "body": "The indeterminate checkbox is a good user experience in many situations and having a checked prop that is not boolean would be weird.\r\n\r\nSince there is an indeterminate property on a checkbox it would be intuitive that any other element with an indeterminate value would have an indeterminate property.\r\n\r\nOne situation that would benefit from an indeterminate property is when needing to toggle an indeterminate state without changing the value. Setting the indeterminate property to true after a few seconds if one section is taking too long and you could still check the value of the progress bar without needing to store the value somewhere else. When that section is finished you could increment the value and the indeterminate property would automatically be set to false until the value attribute is removed or the indeterminate property is set to true.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
