    "created_at": "2017-07-06T14:49:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-07-06T14:49:43Z",
    "body": "I realize you think this would be convenient and a good user experience. But you have not shown this to be the case sufficiently, beyond your personal opinion.\r\n\r\nLet's take a step back way from you proposing a specific API and follow the [process for adding new features](https://wiki.whatwg.org/wiki/FAQ#Is_there_a_process_for_adding_new_features_to_a_specification.3F). What underlying problem are you trying to solve? What use case does it address for users? How can it be done today?\r\n\r\nFrom what I can tell the problem you're trying to solve is \"how do I make progress elements indeterminate\". The standard already has a mechanism for doing this, as was pointed out to you immediately. At that point you're stalled in the process, and we need to close this issue unless you can explain an actual problem that we don't already have a solution for.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
