    "body": "Thank you @domenic \r\n\r\nSorry for being impetuous. I didn't know exactly where to start. I will take a look at the FAQ.\r\n\r\n> The standard already has a mechanism for doing this, as was pointed out to you immediately. At that point you're stalled in the process, and we need to close this issue unless you can explain an actual problem that we don't already have a solution for.\r\n\r\nIs there such thing as a problem that we don't already have a solution for? A `<div>` with css and javascript can do pretty much everything (as the React community has shown)\r\n\r\nWould making the DOM API more intuitive not be a good enough reason to update it?",
